From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: guacamole_nura proposal <TODO-set-author@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: misc: add goodix_fp for the OnePlus 7 Pro optical
 fingerprint sensor

The OnePlus 7 Pro (guacamole) has a Goodix under-display optical sensor
(G_OPTICAL_18821_G2_4). Its data path belongs to a Goodix app in Qualcomm
TrustZone, so Linux only handles power (TLMM 101), reset (TLMM 131) and
the interrupt (TLMM 118).

The stock fingerprint HAL (libgf_ud_hal_18821_G2_4_oplus.so) drives the
sensor through the downstream OnePlus driver's interface. Keep that
interface so the HAL can run unmodified:

 - /dev/goodix_fp with the GF_IOC_* ioctls (magic 'g', numbers 0-23);
 - netlink protocol 25: the HAL registers its port by sending any
   message, and receives one-byte events (IRQ, screen on/off, touch
   down/up, UI ready/disappear);
 - /proc/fp_id, /proc/lcd_type, /proc/fp_kernel_event (reads 1:
   netlink, the non-GKI mode) and /proc/tee_bind_core.

Downstream, the touchscreen and display drivers report the finger over
the sensor and the lit spot. Mainline has no such hooks, so the device
takes them from userspace through the sysfs attributes touch, ui_ready
and screen.

Closing the last file descriptor disables the interrupt and powers the
sensor off, so a HAL that dies mid-capture does not leave it powered.

Interface source: LineageOS android_kernel_oneplus_sm8150 (lineage-23.2),
drivers/input/oplus_fp_drivers/goodix_optical_fp/gf_spi.[ch],
gf_netlink.c, gf_platform.c and oplus_fp_common/. Not upstreamable as
is: the compatible and /proc nodes are the downstream ABI.
---
 drivers/input/misc/Kconfig     |  13 +
 drivers/input/misc/Makefile    |   1 +
 drivers/input/misc/goodix_fp.c | 521 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 535 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/misc/goodix_fp.c

